    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d426">

                <pb facs="0578" n="472" xml:id="pg472"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Abbott</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-01-16"><hi rendition="#italic">January 16,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 145.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 164, of the 17th
                    ultimo, in regard to the interpretation of section 10 of article <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi> of the consular convention of 1850 between
                    the United States and Colombia, relating to the administration of the estates of
                    deceased persons by consular officers.</p>
                <p>I approve the tenor of your note on the subject to Señor Roldán.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
